  "title": "Weddings in Georgia",
  "date": "02-20",
  "text": "Title: Weddings in Georgia\n\nAbout ten minutes after my plane landed in Tbilisi, I had three weddings to go to. There was Wi-Fi in the airport, and as I stood in line at passport control I paged through two e-mails delivering the excited news that village weddings had been discovered, and that, in accordance with the old Georgian saying “A guest is a gift from God,” I was to be an honored visitor at each. Some of the Georgians I had reached out to before the trip had mentioned that it was actually sort of hard to go to Georgia and not find yourself invited to one wedding or another",
